<title>GERMANY: D. Babcock BSH unit to omit dividend.</title>
<headline>D. Babcock BSH unit to omit dividend.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Sept 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>						  1995/96	 1994/95</p>
<p> 15.6 profit</p>
<p>    Group incoming orders		    719    vs  772.8</p>
<p>    Group sales				  832    vs  763.7</p>
<p>    Group overall output		     835    vs  822.9</p>
<p>    Dividend					 0    vs   10 marks</p>
<p>    Group workforce			  2,621    vs 2,779</p>
<p>NOTE - The full name of the Deutsche Babcock unit is Babcock-BSH AG. The reported 1995/96 results are pretax, and preliminary. The forecast loss stems mainly from one-time costs such as restructuring.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
